{"surah": 1, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ ", "translation": "In the name of Allāh,[1] the Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful.[2]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "بِسْمِ", "translit": "ِmْsِb", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱللَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّllٱ", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ", "translit": "ِnَٰmْḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ ", "translation": "[All] praise is [due] to Allāh, Lord[1] of the worlds -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلْحَمْدُ", "translit": "ُdْmَḥْlٱ", "root": "حمد"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِلَّهِ", "translit": "ِhَّlِl", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبِّ", "translit": "ِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ", "translit": "َnyِmَlَٰʿعْlٱ", "root": "علم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ ", "translation": "The Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ", "translit": "ِnَٰmْḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلرَّحِيمِ", "translit": "ِmyِḥَّrlٱ", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ ", "translation": "Sovereign of the Day of Recompense.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "مَٰلِكِ", "translit": "ِkِlَٰm", "root": "ملك"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَوْمِ", "translit": "ِmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلدِّينِ", "translit": "ِnyِّdlٱ", "root": "دين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ ", "translation": "It is You we worship and You we ask for help.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِيَّاكَ", "translit": "َkāَّyِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَعْبُدُ", "translit": "ُdُbْʿعَn", "root": "عبد"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَإِيَّاكَ", "translit": "َkāَّyِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "نَسْتَعِينُ", "translit": "ُnyِʿعَtْsَn", "root": "عون"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ ", "translation": "Guide us to the straight path -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱهْدِنَا", "translit": "āَnِdْhٱ", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلصِّرَٰطَ", "translit": "َṭَٰrِّṣlٱ", "root": "صرط"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِqَtْsُmْlٱ", "root": "قوم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "صِرَٰطَ ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ غَيْرِ ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا ٱلضَّآلِّينَ ", "translation": "The path of those upon whom You have bestowed favor, not of those who have earned [Your] anger or of those who are astray.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "صِرَٰطَ", "translit": "َṭَٰrِṣ", "root": "صرط"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَنْعَمْتَ", "translit": "َtْmَʿعْnَaʾ", "root": "نعم"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "غَيْرِ", "translit": "ِrْyَغ", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ", "translit": "ِbwُḍْغَmْlٱ", "root": "غضب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "ٱلضَّآلِّينَ", "translit": "َnyِّlٓāَّḍlٱ", "root": "ضلل"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"3": [{"arabic": "الله لا إله إلا أنا مبدىء كل شيء وإلي يعود العزيز الحكيم الرحمن الرحيم مالك يوم الدين خالق الخير والشر خالق الجنة والنار الواحد الأحد الفرد الصمد الذي لم يتخذ صاحبة ولا ولدا الفرد الوتر عالم الغيب والشهادة الملك القدوس السلام المؤمن المهيمن العزيز الجبار المتكبر الخالق البارىء المصور الكبير المتعال المقتدر القهار الحليم الكريم أهل الثناء والمجد أعلم السر وأخفى القادر الرزاق فوق الخلق والخليقة (1) وذكر قبل كل كلمة إني أنا الله لا إله إلا أنا كما أوردناه في الأول فمن دعا بهذه الأسماء فليقل إنك أنت الله لا إله إلا أنت كذا و", "english": "Muḥammad ibn Ḥassān said: Maʿrūf al-Karkhī — may God have mercy on him — said to me: \"Shall I not teach you ten words — five for this world and five for the Hereafter? Whoever supplicates God — Mighty and Majestic — with them shall find God — Most High — present with them.\" I said: \"Write them down for me.\" He said: \"No, but I shall repeat them to you as Bakr ibn Khunays — may God have mercy on him — repeated them to me:", "book_title": "On Invocations and Supplications", "section_title_ar": "Section 249", "section_title_en": "Section 249 — Supplications of the Righteous (Adʿiyat al-Ṣāliḥīn)", "section_index": 249, "anchors": "- Root: حسب (ḥ-s-b)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of counting, reckoning, and sufficiency — \"ḥasb\" denotes that which suffices or is enough\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الحساب: استعمال العدد\" — the theological nuance of ḥasbī Allāh (\"God is my Sufficer\") carries the sense of complete reliance upon God's reckoning and provision, transcending mere numerical counting to signify total trust in divine sufficiency\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah): \"حسب المال\" (he counted the wealth); Metaphorical (majāz): \"خرجا يتحسبان الأخبار\" (they go out seeking news) — in the supplication \"ḥasbī Allāh,\" the literal sense of \"sufficiency\" is intended, yet it carries the metaphorical extension of complete trust, as one who has God as his Sufficer has no need of any other reckoning\n\n- Root: اله (ʾ-l-h)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning of worship, devotion, and seeking refuge; \"ilāh\" denotes that which is worshipped\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الله: قيل: أصله إله فحذفت همزته، وأدخل عليها الألف واللام، فخص بالباري تعالى\" — the name Allāh is the proper name of the Creator, distinguished from generic \"ilāh\" (any object of worship); in these supplications, the divine names invoked (al-Karīm, al-Ḥalīm, al-Qawī, al-Shadīd, al-Raḥīm, al-Raʾūf, al-Laṭīf, al-Qadīr) each specify particular attributes of the divine essence\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"فلان يتأله: يتعبد\" (he worships); the supplications employ the divine names in their literal theological sense, each name invoking a specific attribute relevant to the particular need mentioned\n\n- Root: انا (ʾ-n-y)\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"أنا ضمير المخبر عن نفسه\" — the first-person pronoun; in the divine self-declaration \"innī anā Allāh,\" the repetition emphasizes divine self-identification\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: \"أنى الطعام أي إدراكه\" (the food ripened/reached its time) — the related sense of something reaching its appointed time appears in \"عند المسألة في القبر\" (at the questioning in the grave), indicating appointed moments of divine reckoning\n\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الفصل بين الجار والمجرور (Prepositional Interposition) — The supplications employ repeated prepositional phrases (ʿinda al-mawt, ʿinda al-masʾalah, ʿinda al-ḥisāb, ʿinda al-mīzān, ʿinda al-ṣirāṭ) in parallel construction, each governing a distinct divine name, creating a rhythmic liturgical structure where each clause stands as an independent invocation\n\n---\n\n##", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the journey of the soul, death, and the Hereafter, from 'On Invocations and Supplications'", "badge": "Afterlife"}]}, "wordTiming": {"minshawi": {"1": [[1, 550, 1071], [2, 1071, 1744], [3, 1744, 2921], [4, 2921, 4200]], "1:1": [[1, 550, 1071], [2, 1071, 1744], [3, 1744, 2921], [4, 2921, 4200]], "2": [[1, 760, 1699], [2, 1699, 2469], [3, 2469, 3049], [4, 3049, 4950]], "1:2": [[1, 760, 1699], [2, 1699, 2469], [3, 2469, 3049], [4, 3049, 4950]], "3": [[1, 770, 2146], [2, 2146, 3640]], "1:3": [[1, 770, 2146], [2, 2146, 3640]], "4": [[1, 790, 1483], [2, 1483, 2395], [3, 2395, 3580]], "1:4": [[1, 790, 1483], [2, 1483, 2395], [3, 2395, 3580]], "5": [[1, 970, 2265], [2, 2265, 2870], [3, 2870, 4507], [4, 4507, 5610]], "1:5": [[1, 970, 2265], [2, 2265, 2870], [3, 2870, 4507], [4, 4507, 5610]], "6": [[1, 870, 1832], [2, 1832, 2897], [3, 2897, 4360]], "1:6": [[1, 870, 1832], [2, 1832, 2897], [